  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 608.04 Beach Nourishment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 608.04 Beach Nourishment.\n\n(a) Beach nourishment shall be:\n\n(1) Allowed only on publicly-owned beaches; and\n\n(2) Authorized only by the state or local agency responsible for maintaining the beach.\n\n(b) Proposed nourishment material shall be:\n\n(1) Chosen based on compatibility with that of existing beach material for grain size, shape, and color; and\n\n(2) If not virgin material, tested for contaminants prior to placement on the beach.\n\n(c) The slope of the beach after beach nourishment shall mimic the natural beach profile.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
